### SheafNMA (2026-05-12; v0.2.0 real-NMA-corpus validation + 36-cell Ã— 1000-rep simulation + methods paper draft)
> - `C:\Models\SheafNMA\` â€” cellular-sheaf inconsistency localization for network meta-analysis. v0.1.0 (2026-04-07) was math + single-file HTML dashboard + E156 #153 micro-paper on a synthetic 12-contrast network. v0.2.0 refactored the 457-LOC `generate_figures.py` into a `sheafnma/` package (`core`, `io`, `simulate`, `comparators`, `r_bridge`), validated on 13 R-netmeta built-in NMAs, and shipped a methods-paper draft for Research Synthesis Methods.
> - Method: precision-weighted coboundary `F[e, treat1] = -1/SE_e, F[e, treat2] = +1/SE_e`; sheaf Laplacian `L = Fáµ€F` (symmetric PSD); WLS-solve node estimates with node 0 anchored; per-edge residuals `r_e = dÌƒ_e âˆ’ (F x*)_e` localize inconsistency; **Global Inconsistency Index** `GII = Î£ rÂ²` is the global statistic. One algebraic object yields both global + per-edge â€” complements (not replaces) node-splitting.
> - Real-corpus headline: across **13 R-netmeta built-in NMAs** (Senn 2013 diabetes, Dias smokingcessation, Dong 2013 thrombolytics, Linde 2015/2016 acupuncture, Salanti antimanic, Baker, Dogliotti, Franchini, Gurusamy, Stowe, Woods, dietaryfat, parkinson) the global design-by-treatment Ï‡Â² (Higgins 2012) failed to reject in all 13. **SheafNMA flagged â‰¥1 localized inconsistency edge in 5 of those 13 (38.5%)** at the Youden-frozen threshold of **2.6912** â€” networks that look globally consistent harbor at least one inconsistent edge the global test misses.
> - Simulation rigor: 36-cell grid (n_treatments âˆˆ {4,6,8} Ã— n_studies_per_edge âˆˆ {3,5,10} Ã— Ï„_inc âˆˆ {0,0.2,0.5,1.0}) Ã— **1000 replications per cell**, held-out training cell at (6,5,0.5) for Youden's-J threshold selection (frozen before evaluating remaining 35 cells). Type-I error at Ï„_inc=0 was **0.000 across all cells**. Mean per-edge sensitivity 0.981 / specificity 0.945 at Ï„_inc=0.5.
> - Comparator suite: DBT-Ï‡Â² (Higgins 2012 Â§3.2, pure-Python), Bucher loop closure (Bucher 1997, pure-Python), node-splitting (Dias 2010, via `netmeta::netsplit` shelled to R 4.5.2). Per-edge agreement with node-splitting was 45.4% â€” asymmetric: SheafNMA flags 12/506 = 2.4% of edges vs node-splitting's 250/436 = 57% at p<0.05 Bonferroni-uncorrected (the calibrated Youden cut is much more conservative than a per-edge Î±-test). Â§4.2 of the paper explicitly explains this rather than presenting the 45.4% bare.
> - Corpus export: `corpus/export_netmeta.R` handles 7 distinct netmeta dataset formats (contrast-level TE/seTE, arm-based event/n, arm-based mean/sd/n, wide multi-arm OR/MD, three-arm smokingcessation, rate-based IRR/person-years) and exports all 13 to `corpus/data/*.csv` in the sheafnma standard schema (`study, treat1, treat2, effect, se`).
> - GitHub: `https://github.com/mahmood726-cyber/sheaf-nma` (master `6c7db13`, tag `v0.2.0`). Pages LIVE: `https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/sheaf-nma/` (Phase-1 dashboard unchanged in v0.2). 33 tests passing; Sentinel BLOCK=0 WARN=0 (2 INFO = pre-existing HTML a11y items in the v0.1 dashboard).
> - Workbook entry: `[153/919] SheafNMA`. CURRENT BODY updated 2026-05-12 to the v0.2 156-word / 7-sentence body (replaces v0.1 synthetic-"smoking cessation" framing with the real netmeta corpus). SUBMITTED `[ ]`; YOUR REWRITE preserved untouched per workbook protection rules. Target: Research Synthesis Methods full methods paper (`paper/sheafnma_v2.md`, 1190 words drafted; [TODO] prose blocks in Â§1 Background / Â§4.3 case studies / Â§5 Discussion) + SynthÄ“sis Methods Note companion (`paper/methods_note.md`, 156-word).
> - Known landmine: `Dong2013` netsplit fails inside netmeta's multi-arm validator ("wrong number of comparisons"); SheafNMA + DBT + Bucher still run on it, only `netsplit_p` column is blank for its 70 edges.
> - v0.2 deferrals (spec Â§10): multi-arm covariance correction (single-D stalks only), higher-D stalks (Phase 1 Â§3.4 future work), Bayesian sheaf priors, OTS / Bitcoin anchor (broken on Py 3.13 Windows per `lessons.md`).

### hksj-q-floor-atlas (2026-05-12; 8th Pairwise70 atlas; tags prereg-v0.0.1 + v0.1.0)
> - `C:\Projects\hksj-q-floor-atlas\` â€” 8th calibration atlas in the Pairwise70 series. Sister to `cochrane-modern-re` (engine source), `repro-floor-atlas`, `responder-floor-atlas`, `trial-truthfulness-atlas`, `africa-tb-atlas`, `pactr-hiddenness-atlas`, `africa-hiv-prep-atlas`.
> - Question: how often does omitting the `max(1, Q/(k-1))` floor on HKSJ variance, in the I^2=0 regime where un-floored HKSJ narrows below REML+Wald, overstate precision across the Cochrane CDSR? Pre-registered via `prereg-v0.0.1` tag + 4 Internet Archive snapshots (Bitcoin OTS deferred â€” Python 3.13 SSL libeay32 bug per lessons.md; web-stamper fallback documented).
> - Headline: D_1 (I^2=0, k>=2, converged) = 3,677 MAs = 57.6% of corpus. On D_1a (Q>0, n=3,536): median CI-width ratio (floored / un-floored) = 3.64x (IQR 1.60-10.56; 95th pct 57.4x); significance lost in 17.08% of MAs. D_1b (Q=0, n=141 = 3.83% of D_1): sig_loss 24.8%, ratio unbounded â€” un-floored HKSJ SE is exactly zero (the floor effect is unbounded); see `docs/AMENDMENTS.md` entry 1 for split rationale.
> - Per k-stratum medians: k=2: 4.26x (sig_loss 8.6%); k=3: 3.64x (12.9%); k=4-5: 3.10x (13.1%); k=6-9: 3.18x (17.3%); k>=10: 3.80x (25.1%). sig_loss increases with k because higher-k pooled effects sit closer to null, so floor widening crosses zero more often.
> - Engine: independent metafor pass via fork of cochrane-modern-re's `run_metafor.R` minus the floor block. Input parquet SHA-256 pinned in `docs/spec.md` sec.1.5 (`31434fb118c6ec44a025eeb43a90e35ef9e050711fa45aa2cb5c1244b2d89751`). 3 hand-verified golden MAs match metafor reference within 1e-6.
> - GitHub: `https://github.com/mahmood726-cyber/hksj-q-floor-atlas` (master + tags `prereg-v0.0.1` and `v0.1.0`). Pages LIVE: `https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/hksj-q-floor-atlas/`.
> - 64 tests; Sentinel BLOCK=0 WARN=0 INFO=0; 7 IA snapshots recorded in `docs/preregistration.md`.
> - Workbook entry: `[920/920] hksj-q-floor-atlas`; target SynthÄ“sis Methods Note (340w draft, â‰¤400 cap).
> - v0.2 candidates (NOT in v0.1.0): published-CI matching ("is THIS Cochrane review wrong?"), PM/SJ/Bayesian Ï„Â² robustness, DL re-pooling, Bitcoin OTS once Python 3.13 issue is resolved.

